<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TV-side copy for the third diagnosis: the bytes arrived and this TV cannot decode
  them. Kept in its own file because res/values merges every file in the directory,
  so this cannot collide with edits to strings.xml. Keys are prefixed
  error_unplayable_ and exist nowhere else.

  The wording never blames the phone, because in this case the phone was serving
  correctly — that mistake is the whole reason this diagnosis exists. It also never
  offers a retry: nothing about a second attempt gives this TV a decoder it does not
  have, and the sender owns the retry affordance in any case.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="error_unplayable_title">This TV can\'t play this video</string>
    <string name="error_unplayable_detail">The file reached the TV fine — its video format isn\'t one this TV can decode. Your phone is still connected, so you can pick something else and cast again.</string>
</resources>
